  "stem": "The expression \\((x - 4)(x + 9)\\) is equivalent to \\(x^{2} + bx + c\\), where \\(b\\) and \\(c\\) are constants. What is the value of \\(c\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "-36"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Multiply each term: \\(x \\cdot x + 9x - 4x + (-4)(9)\\).",
    "Combine like terms: \\(x^{2} + 5x - 36\\), so \\(c = -36\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
